===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-}}
Allegedly coined by sexologist {{w|Richard von Krafft-Ebing}} who had already used {{l|en|cunnilingus}} in such a sense of denoting the practice instead of its actor and spread by the tenth edition of ''Psychopathia sexualis'' of 1898 (English edition page [https://archive.org/details/sexualispsychopathia00kraf/page/185/mode 185], German edition page [https://archive.org/details/b20406654/page/124 124], referencing a description of his in ''Centralblatt für die Krankheiten der Harn- und Sexual-Organe'' Vol. VI of 1895 pages [https://archive.org/details/centralblattfrd14unkngoog/page/n390 355–357]). However that usage of this word is just one incidental one and such an attribution may be transferred from the observation of other sexological terms having spread by Krafft-Ebing’s book. Likely independently coined at various occasions by analogy to more frequently known {{m|en|cunnilingus}}, that is a translingual {{blend|en|anus|cunnilingus|nocap=1}}.

